{
  "id": "f1-alphabet",
  "title": "The Alphabet",
  "summary": "All 28 letters, their names, sounds, and joined forms.",
  "quizMode": "ar-en",
  "hideVocab": true,
  "sections": [
    { "type": "text", "body": "<p>Arabic is written <strong>right to left</strong> and has 28 letters, all consonants. Vowels are mostly shown with small marks, which you'll learn next lesson.</p><p>Most letters <strong>connect</strong> to the letter after them, so each letter has up to four shapes: on its own, at the start of a word, in the middle, and at the end. The core shape stays recognizable.</p>" },
    { "type": "note", "body": "Six letters never connect to the letter after them: <span class='ar' lang='ar'>ا د ذ ر ز و</span>. A word breaks after each of them, which is why some words look like they have gaps." },
    { "type": "heading", "text": "The 28 letters" },
    { "type": "letters", "items": [
      { "ar": "ا", "name": "alif", "sound": "long a; carries hamza" },
      { "ar": "ب", "name": "bāʼ", "sound": "b as in boy" },
      { "ar": "ت", "name": "tāʼ", "sound": "t as in tea" },
      { "ar": "ث", "name": "thāʼ", "sound": "th as in think" },
      { "ar": "ج", "name": "jīm", "sound": "j as in jam" },
      { "ar": "ح", "name": "ḥāʼ", "sound": "breathy h from the throat" },
      { "ar": "خ", "name": "khāʼ", "sound": "kh as in Scottish loch" },
      { "ar": "د", "name": "dāl", "sound": "d as in door" },
      { "ar": "ذ", "name": "dhāl", "sound": "th as in this" },
      { "ar": "ر", "name": "rāʼ", "sound": "rolled r" },
      { "ar": "ز", "name": "zāy", "sound": "z as in zoo" },
      { "ar": "س", "name": "sīn", "sound": "s as in sun" },
      { "ar": "ش", "name": "shīn", "sound": "sh as in ship" },
      { "ar": "ص", "name": "ṣād", "sound": "heavy (emphatic) s" },
      { "ar": "ض", "name": "ḍād", "sound": "heavy (emphatic) d" },
      { "ar": "ط", "name": "ṭāʼ", "sound": "heavy (emphatic) t" },
      { "ar": "ظ", "name": "ẓāʼ", "sound": "heavy th as in this" },
      { "ar": "ع", "name": "ʿayn", "sound": "voiced squeeze in the throat" },
      { "ar": "غ", "name": "ghayn", "sound": "gargled r, like French r" },
      { "ar": "ف", "name": "fāʼ", "sound": "f as in fish" },
      { "ar": "ق", "name": "qāf", "sound": "deep k from the back of the throat" },
      { "ar": "ك", "name": "kāf", "sound": "k as in kite" },
      { "ar": "ل", "name": "lām", "sound": "l as in light" },
      { "ar": "م", "name": "mīm", "sound": "m as in moon" },
      { "ar": "ن", "name": "nūn", "sound": "n as in noon" },
      { "ar": "ه", "name": "hāʼ", "sound": "h as in hat" },
      { "ar": "و", "name": "wāw", "sound": "w, or long ū" },
      { "ar": "ي", "name": "yāʼ", "sound": "y, or long ī" }
    ] },
    { "type": "note", "body": "Learn letters in <strong>families</strong> that share a shape and differ only by dots: <span class='ar' lang='ar'>ب ت ث</span>, <span class='ar' lang='ar'>ج ح خ</span>, <span class='ar' lang='ar'>د ذ</span>, <span class='ar' lang='ar'>ر ز</span>, <span class='ar' lang='ar'>س ش</span>, <span class='ar' lang='ar'>ص ض</span>, <span class='ar' lang='ar'>ط ظ</span>, <span class='ar' lang='ar'>ع غ</span>." }
  ],
